<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY MARCH PMI INDEX 55.1PCT VS 50.4PCT IN FEB.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY MARCH PMI INDEX 55.1PCT VS 50.4PCT IN FEB.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Purchasing Manager</p>
<p>Index (PMI) was 55.1 percent in March, up from 50.4 percent in</p>
<p>February, the Hungarian Association of Logistics, Purchasing</p>
<p>and Inventory Management (HALPIM) said on Friday.</p>
<p>The following is a history of the index over the year on a</p>
<p>month-to-month basis:</p>
<p>PURCHASING MANAGER INDEX (Percent)</p>
<p>    1997 March		    55.1</p>
<p>	   February		 50.4</p>
<p>	   January		  46.0</p>
<p>    1996 December		 44.7</p>
<p>	   November		 52.8</p>
<p>	   October		  57.8</p>
<p>	   September		60.4</p>
<p>	   August		   52.7</p>
<p>	   July		     48.5</p>
<p>	   June		     50.6</p>
<p>	   May			53.8</p>
<p>	   April		    51.4</p>
<p>	   March		    51.4</p>
<p>NOTE: The PMI is calculated using the same methodology as</p>
<p>the United States' National Association of Purchasing</p>
<p>Management Index. A figure above 50 indicates increasing</p>
<p>economic activity, while a number below 50 shows declining</p>
<p>economic activity</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
